  "summary": "A former Costa Mesa police officer, Robert Jay Josett, pleaded guilty to misdemeanors after using law enforcement tools including Flock ALPR cameras and CLETS to track his wife, mistress, and her romantic interests. He was sentenced to three years probation and a 52-week domestic violence program, and was fired by Costa Mesa PD in June 2024.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "He is also accused of using FLOCK license plate readers to track his mistress and her romantic interests.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "No one should have to live in fear of being tracked through law enforcement databases by someone with a badge and a gun because they decided to call off a romantic relationship",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
  ],
